  "step_3": "The decision reason requires identifying which lottery is more right-skewed (i.e., assigns higher probability to its unfavorable outcome) and preferring that one. Lottery A is more right-skewed (90% on -3000) than B (45% on -6000), so the reason would select A. However, the individual chose B and justified this by preferring the higher chance of the best outcome (0), which reflects a preference for higher probability of the least bad outcome, not a preference for more right-skewed distributions. The individual considered the probabilities of the best outcome and compared the risk of large vs. certain losses, but did not reference or appear to assess the overall shape or skewness of the distributions. There is no indication that they evaluated which lottery concentrates more probability on its unfavorable outcome. Instead, they favored the lottery with more probability on the favorable outcome, which is the opposite of what the skewness reason prescribes. Therefore, the individual's reasoning contradicts the decision reason rather than aligning with it.",
